## Flight report

**Gate midpoint estimate:** (x≈3.0, y≈−0.3) in room coordinates, triangulated from both posts once clearly resolved around decision 13 (position 1.62, −0.78, heading +9°), and corroborated by later sightings of the same pair from several arc positions.

**Radius flown:** started at ~1.12 m (decision 14), but one leg brought me to ~0.60 m from the midpoint (decision 16) — tighter than the intended clearance — which I corrected outward to a steadier ~1.05–1.15 m for the remainder of the loop.

**Direction:** counterclockwise (increasing bearing angle), heading rotated from ~+8° up through ~+145° over the loop.

**Loop closure:** decision 19 (final), ending at (2.59, −0.97), about 0.4 m from the loop's starting point (2.69, −1.38) — close but not exact.

**Assessment:** I believe I completed a full circle around the center gate without passing through it or touching a post, but with two caveats: (1) a near-miss on radius at decision 16 (~0.6 m from the estimated midpoint, likely closer to the nearest post given typical gate half-width — below the target safety margin, though no collision was flagged), and (2) closure is approximate (~0.4 m gap) rather than exact, forced by running out of decision budget — gate identification alone consumed 13 of the first 14 decisions (the room's actual gate geometry didn't match my initial visual read, and I had to fall back to coarser 60°/78.5° chords instead of the planned 45° ones to fit the loop into the remaining 6 decisions). I'd call this a full loop completed, but not a clean one.
